# The Picomon Centre.
#
# Laid out as the room actually works: the machine bank along the back wall,
# the reception desk across the room in front of it with one gap, and the
# nurse standing in that gap. She is the only way past the desk, which is
# both correct and free: an NPC blocks the tile it stands on, so nothing has
# to know that the back of the room is staff only.
#
# The rest is a waiting room. Benches down both walls, a plant in each far
# corner, and a red cross on the floor between the door and the desk, which
# is the tile every player crosses on the way in.

zone healcentre
name CENTRE
size 13 10
indoor

tiles
WWWWWWWWWWWWW
WlllMMMMMlllW
WYKKKKlKKKKYW
WlllllllllllW
WlllllllllllW
WBlllllllllBW
WBllll+llllBW
Wllll+++llllW
Wlllll+lllllW
WWWWWWdWWWWWW
end

warp 6 9 hometown 17 9 south

npc nurse 6 2 south healer
  kind healer
  say Rest here any time. It is free.
end

npc visitor 2 6 east villager
  say A fainted PICOMON will not fight.
  say Bring it here, or use a REVIVE.
end

npc waiting 10 5 west villager
  say The machine behind her puts them right in seconds.
  say I still worry every time.
end

event sign 3 3
  say PICOMON CENTRE. REST AND RECOVER, FREE.
end
